.TH WORKSPACE-ZONES 7 "2026-11-10" "waybar-workspace-buttons" "Hyprland"
.SH NAME
workspace-zones \- per-workspace scratch zones for Hyprland
.SH DESCRIPTION
A workspace zone gives every numeric workspace its own scratch area:
workspace
.I N
owns
.IR special:N .
Leaving a workspace closes its zone, no matter how the switch happened
(keybind, bar click,
.BR hyprctl ).
.PP
Zones are a few lines of Lua in the Hyprland config. They need Hyprland
0.57 or newer with the Lua config
.RI ( hyprland.lua ),
and they need no compositor plugin. hypr-DE ships them in its packaged
config. The Waybar CFFI module in this package only draws the has-special
dot on workspace buttons; that dot is what these zones were built for.
.PP
Until waybar-workspace-buttons 1.5.0 zones came from a compiled Hyprland
plugin of the same name. It was retired because it had to be rebuilt for
every Hyprland release and its package pinned an exact Hyprland version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.nf
local zones = {}

-- The numbered workspace on the focused monitor, or nil.
local function zone_owner()
    local ws = hl.get_active_workspace()
    return ws and ws.id or nil
end

function zones.toggle()
    local id = zone_owner()
    if id then hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.workspace.toggle_special(tostring(id))) end
end

function zones.move(follow)
    local id = zone_owner()
    if id then
        hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.window.move({ workspace = "special:" .. id, follow = follow }))
    end
end

hl.bind("SUPER + ALT + S",         function() zones.toggle() end)
hl.bind("SUPER + ALT + SHIFT + S", function() zones.move(true) end)
hl.bind("SUPER + CTRL + ALT + S",  function() zones.move(false) end)

hl.config({ binds = { hide_special_on_workspace_change = true } })
.fi
.TP
.B zones.toggle()
Show or hide this workspace's zone.
.TP
.B zones.move(true)
Send the focused window to the zone and follow it.
.TP
.B zones.move(false)
Stash the focused window without following.
.PP
A named workspace has no numeric id, so it owns no zone and the three
functions do nothing there.
.SH DISMISSAL
.B binds:hide_special_on_workspace_change = true
is what closes a zone when its workspace is left. It is a built-in Hyprland
option, scoped to the target workspace's monitor, so a special open on
another monitor stays. It also covers switching to the workspace already
underneath the special.
.PP
The option applies to every special workspace, so it closes a named
scratchpad such as
.I special:magic
as well. Set it to false to keep zones and scratchpads open across
workspace switches. The plugin's
.B plugin:workspace-zones:auto_dismiss
option no longer exists.
.SH SEE ALSO
